# Exclude everything; re-include only what the image needs.
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. A denylist would have to remember the ~1.2 GB
# host .venv/, .git/, data/, docs/build/, every cache dir, and -- critically --
# the top-level `manuscript` entry, which is a dangling symlink pointing outside
# the build context and would break the build outright. An allowlist gets all of
# that right by construction, and stays correct as the repo grows.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!tests/
!conf/base/
!conf/logging.yml

# Re-exclude, inside the allowed subtrees:
**/__pycache__
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
src/*.egg-info
